when I saw Antifa
gathering in the doorways

00:11:07.700 --> 00:11:09.635
just outside the North
lawn of the White House

00:11:09.635 --> 00:11:11.604
the world's press were
pointing their cameras

00:11:11.604 --> 00:11:13.039
at the White House.

00:11:13.039 --> 00:11:15.608 align:start size:94% position:6%
And beside them underneath
some of the doorways

00:11:15.608 --> 00:11:17.209
I saw what was clearly Antifa

00:11:17.209 --> 00:11:19.812
gathering because
they were changing

00:11:19.812 --> 00:11:21.814
into clothes so that they
couldn't be recognized

00:11:21.814 --> 00:11:26.519 align:start size:84% position:16%
by CCTV cameras went
over to film this

00:11:26.519 --> 00:11:28.487
'cause it was clear that
this was what was going on

00:11:28.487 --> 00:11:31.323
and they became very
violent, very fast.

00:11:31.323 --> 00:11:36.062
And they are thugs they
are a paramilitary group.

00:11:36.062 --> 00:11:37.997 align:start size:81% position:19%
They have no place
in a democracy

00:11:39.432 --> 00:11:41.667
it's to America's shame that
they've been allowed to do

00:11:41.667 --> 00:11:43.269
what they have been doing.

00:11:43.269 --> 00:11:45.071
They threatened to
kill journalists.

00:11:45.071 --> 00:11:48.874
They had graffitied "kill
Andy Ngo" mutual friend

00:11:48.874 --> 00:11:52.044 align:start size:97% position:3%
and a journalist and
reporter in Portland, Oregon.

00:11:52.044 --> 00:11:56.248
They had graffitied calls to
murder him across the city.

00:11:57.883 --> 00:12:00.619 align:start size:97% position:3%
The fact that they can then
intimidate a journalist

00:12:00.619 --> 00:12:05.324
from abroad who even has the
tenacity to try to capture them

00:12:05.324 --> 00:12:08.594 align:start size:94% position:6%
on the video camera or
look at what they're doing

00:12:08.594 --> 00:12:09.762
is very bad.

00:12:09.762 --> 00:12:11.163 align:start size:84% position:16%
Is an embarrassment
from America.

00:12:11.163 --> 00:12:12.698 align:start size:94% position:6%
I think the whole
thing's an embarrassment.

00:12:12.698 --> 00:12:15.134
- Did you get a sense that
when you're on the ground

00:12:15.134 --> 00:12:17.169 align:start size:81% position:19%
with them that
there is a leader?

00:12:17.169 --> 00:12:20.973 align:start size:97% position:3%
Because this is what Joe Biden
described Antifa as an idea

00:12:20.973 --> 00:12:23.409 align:start size:88% position:13%
and partly what I
think it seems to be is

00:12:23.409 --> 00:12:27.046 align:start size:97% position:3%
that there's no sort of known
leader sort of by design

00:12:27.046 --> 00:12:29.448 align:start size:97% position:3%
but when you're out there
with these groups, DC Portland

00:12:29.448 --> 00:12:31.684 align:start size:84% position:16%
wherever you are,
could you sense like,

00:12:31.684 --> 00:12:33.319 align:start size:81% position:19%
Oh somebody is
actually in charge

00:12:33.319 --> 00:12:35.187
or is it just like
this roving gang?

00:12:35.187 --> 00:12:36.655
Yeah

00:12:36.655 --> 00:12:39.024
- No, of course they
have a leadership.

00:12:39.024 --> 00:12:41.827
Andy Ngo's forthcoming book
will reveal a lot about this

00:12:42.962 --> 00:12:44.830 align:start size:88% position:13%
but yeah, of course
they have a leadership.

00:12:46.031 --> 00:12:49.568
They don't gather like
moisture or something.

00:12:49.568 --> 00:12:52.171
I mean, it's a, they
are brought together.

00:12:52.171 --> 00:12:53.372
They are organized.

00:12:53.372 --> 00:12:55.541 align:start size:84% position:16%
They advertise within
their own groups

00:12:55.541 --> 00:12:56.842
what they're going to do

00:12:56.842 --> 00:12:57.810
and when and what
their actions are.

00:12:57.810 --> 00:13:00.379
They tell people what to bring

00:13:00.379 --> 00:13:02.782
or what not to bring, what
to say and what not to say

00:13:02.782 --> 00:13:05.050
what to chant and
what not to chant.

00:13:05.050 --> 00:13:08.320
And yeah, I mean they
do the whole thing.

00:13:08.320 --> 00:13:10.022
They're an organized group.

00:13:10.022 --> 00:13:12.992 align:start position:0%
And by the way, one of the most
haunting things for me was,

00:13:14.593 --> 00:13:16.262 align:start size:94% position:6%
among other things I
interviewed lots of people

00:13:16.262 --> 00:13:20.332
on my travels including black
police officers in Oregon,

00:13:20.332 --> 00:13:22.468
who I think were
some of the most,

00:13:22.468 --> 00:13:25.004
the bravest most remarkable

00:13:25.004 --> 00:13:29.742 align:start size:88% position:13%
and I thought restrained
people I've ever met.

00:13:31.310 --> 00:13:34.146 align:start size:97% position:3%
But one of the conversations
that haunted me even more

00:13:34.146 --> 00:13:38.083
than that, was speaking to
an owner of a restaurant in,

00:13:38.083 --> 00:13:42.688
a cafe in Portland who
had just recently had

00:13:42.688 --> 00:13:45.891 align:start position:0%
just the day before had had
bullets live ammunition bullets

00:13:45.891 --> 00:13:49.361 align:start size:88% position:13%
fired through the
windows of his business

00:13:49.361 --> 00:13:52.731 align:start size:84% position:16%
because it seemed
because he has photos

00:13:52.731 --> 00:13:55.167
on the wall of first responders,

00:13:55.167 --> 00:14:00.139 align:start size:97% position:3%
a woman soldier, a US soldier,
a man in fireman's uniform.

00:14:02.408 --> 00:14:03.843
And this apparently makes him a

00:14:03.843 --> 00:14:07.179
a representative of the
fascistic American state

00:14:07.179 --> 00:14:08.981
thus live ammunition is fired

00:14:08.981 --> 00:14:12.318
by Antifa BLM activists
through his business.

00:14:12.318 --> 00:14:16.622 align:start position:0%
By the way, he is a black
American, a very proud patriot.

00:14:16.622 --> 00:14:19.291 align:start size:97% position:3%
And he said to me, actually,
we talked about this.

00:14:19.291 --> 00:14:22.328
I said to him, what
do you think of the

00:14:22.328 --> 00:14:24.496 align:start size:84% position:16%
of the them
presidential contender

00:14:24.496 --> 00:14:27.199 align:start size:84% position:16%
Joe Biden's claim that
it's just an idea.

00:14:27.199 --> 00:14:29.468 align:start size:97% position:3%
And he pointed to the
bullet holes in his business

00:14:29.468 --> 00:14:30.603
his windows, and he said,

00:14:30.603 --> 00:14:33.772 align:start size:84% position:16%
" But an idea doesn't
fire bullets."

00:14:34.940 --> 00:14:35.875
- I mean that's it.

00:14:35.875 --> 00:14:37.443
- So, yeah.

00:14:37.443 --> 00:14:40.446 align:start size:81% position:19%
- So what was your
main takeaway?

00:14:40.446 --> 00:14:42.882 align:start size:84% position:16%
Now that now that
you've left our shores

00:14:42.882 --> 00:14:46.318
you got to see sort of the
bipolar nature of America.

00:14:46.318 --> 00:14:50.055
We're still in this sort of
election limbo at the moment,

00:14:50.055 --> 00:14:52.691
millions of people not
celebrate Thanksgiving

00:14:52.691 --> 00:14:54.260
with their families

00:14:54.260 --> 00:14:56.462 align:start size:97% position:3%
because of COVID and
everything else, or the lock

00:14:56.462 --> 00:14:59.632
I should say the lockdowns
more than COVID specifically.

00:14:59.632 --> 00:15:01.333
What's your diagnosis of

00:15:01.333 --> 00:15:03.002 align:start size:84% position:16%
of what we're
going through here?

00:15:04.436 --> 00:15:06.972 align:start size:84% position:16%
- Oh, I think you're
in real trouble.

00:15:06.972 --> 00:15:08.574
I think you're in real trouble.

00:15:10.743 --> 00:15:12.578
All countries are
to some extent.

00:15:12.578 --> 00:15:15.381 align:start size:84% position:16%
I mean, we all have
the COVID layer on top

00:15:15.381 --> 00:15:16.749
of everything else

00:15:16.749 --> 00:15:21.220 align:start size:97% position:3%
and the financial catastrophe
that it constitutes

00:15:22.621 --> 00:15:25.090 align:start size:97% position:3%
my own country has got to find
a way to pay for something

00:15:25.090 --> 00:15:28.560
like 210 billion pounds
spent so far this year

00:15:29.995 --> 00:15:31.897
in the COVID era.

00:15:31.897 --> 00:15:36.902
These sorts of sums very
hard to recoup in taxation

00:15:38.070 --> 00:15:39.605
without crippling our
economy afterwards.

00:15:39.605 --> 00:15:40.873
We've all got a lot of trouble

00:15:40.873 --> 00:15:44.209
and we have this
very testing year.

00:15:44.209 --> 00:15:47.413
We're all in, still
in with lock downs

00:15:47.413 --> 00:15:50.916
and inability to
see our loved ones

00:15:52.117 --> 00:15:54.486
because of a virus
that is serious.

00:15:54.486 --> 00:15:56.288
But I think in my own estimation

00:15:56.288 --> 00:15:59.491
not as bad as the thing we
thought it was at the outset

00:16:00.993 --> 00:16:04.797 align:start position:0%
and there will be a long period
of people arguing over the

00:16:04.797 --> 00:16:08.534
whether we overreacted
or not with this virus

00:16:08.534 --> 00:16:11.070
but all of these things in a way

00:16:11.070 --> 00:16:15.007 align:start size:97% position:3%
seem to reveal underlying
problems in a society as well.

00:16:15.007 --> 00:16:17.209
I've been struck now, I say that

00:16:17.209 --> 00:16:19.845
in my own country there was
a period of political unity

00:16:19.845 --> 00:16:21.880
at the beginning
of the current era.

00:16:23.048 --> 00:16:26.118
We unified as a country
around health service

00:16:26.118 --> 00:16:29.755 align:start size:97% position:3%
our prime minister,
specifically around the queen.

00:16:30.923 --> 00:16:33.392 align:start size:84% position:16%
And it was a very
moving thing actually

00:16:33.392 --> 00:16:35.027 align:start size:84% position:16%
because we'd said
for years in Britain

00:16:35.027 --> 00:16:38.430 align:start size:94% position:6%
we'd had no societal trust
and no points of unity.

00:16:38.430 --> 00:16:40.766 align:start size:88% position:13%
And actually, I thought
we did have some

00:16:40.766 --> 00:16:43.102 align:start size:88% position:13%
we've lost some of it
since perhaps inevitably

00:16:44.336 --> 00:16:48.640 align:start size:84% position:16%
but we did have stores
of trust and unity.

00:16:48.640 --> 00:16:50.609
The one country in
the world I know of

00:16:50.609 --> 00:16:53.779
where that just didn't
last a second was America

00:16:54.947 --> 00:16:56.815
because of the nature
of the Trump presidency

00:16:56.815 --> 00:16:58.384
because of its divisiveness

00:16:58.384 --> 00:17:00.419
because of the era
that America was in

00:17:00.419 --> 00:17:02.621
and because it was
an election year

00:17:02.621 --> 00:17:06.291
you just had no period of unity.

00:17:06.291 --> 00:17:08.794
And I was struck state by state.

00:17:08.794 --> 00:17:12.231 align:start size:94% position:6%
Some States life was going
on for better or worse

00:17:12.231 --> 00:17:16.969 align:start size:94% position:6%
as if the COVID
Coronavirus didn't exist.

00:17:16.969 --> 00:17:19.905
And other States
you were told off

00:17:19.905 --> 00:17:22.274
if you weren't wearing
your mask in the street.

00:17:23.609 --> 00:17:27.146
So and it seemed to be
along political lines

00:17:27.146 --> 00:17:28.580
and I can appreciate that it is,

00:17:28.580 --> 00:17:31.016
but I also lament that in a way

00:17:31.016 --> 00:17:33.419 align:start size:88% position:13%
because it would be good
if America could even

00:17:33.419 --> 00:17:36.989
have a pandemic, but
reminded Americans

00:17:36.989 --> 00:17:39.625
that they're in it
together in some way.

00:17:39.625 --> 00:17:41.627
And you just, you
can't even do that.

00:17:41.627 --> 00:17:43.595
And may I add one other thing?

00:17:45.030 --> 00:17:49.201
The one that worries me most
now about your country is this.

00:17:49.201 --> 00:17:52.671
I think the worry people had

00:17:52.671 --> 00:17:54.139
which is the people in America

00:17:54.139 --> 00:17:58.310 align:start size:97% position:3%
imbibing different information
streams is a kiddie worry

00:17:58.310 --> 00:18:01.213
compared to the real
one you've now got.

00:18:02.448 --> 00:18:04.716
The real one you've now got is

00:18:04.716 --> 00:18:07.152 align:start size:84% position:16%
you don't any longer
agree as a nation

00:18:07.152 --> 00:18:11.990
on what you just saw,
that is terrifying.

00:18:11.990 --> 00:18:13.192
- So...

00:18:13.192 --> 00:18:14.560
- That is absolutely terrible.

00:18:14.560 --> 00:18:16.762
- I've been describing
that as the reality war

00:18:16.762 --> 00:18:19.998
that that is this isn't
about the cultural battle

00:18:19.998 --> 00:18:21.467 align:start size:84% position:16%
this isn't about the
political battle.

00:18:21.467 --> 00:18:22.935
Those are, those are battles.

00:18:22.935 --> 00:18:26.171 align:start size:97% position:3%
Those are sort of small
battles, but it's all framed

00:18:26.171 --> 00:18:28.774 align:start size:88% position:13%
by the reality war,
which is nobody agrees.

00:18:28.774 --> 00:18:31.243 align:start size:84% position:16%
And even in we're
holding this interview

00:18:31.243 --> 00:18:32.478
for just two or three days

00:18:32.478 --> 00:18:34.780
the amount of stuff
that could change

00:18:34.780 --> 00:18:37.349 align:start size:84% position:16%
in two or three
days even is crazy.

00:18:37.349 --> 00:18:38.717
But you know, when
you mention the sort

00:18:38.717 --> 00:18:40.786
of the way we do lock
downs, I'm reminded

00:18:40.786 --> 00:18:44.456 align:start size:84% position:16%
we went out for lunch
a different day,
and we were sitting

00:18:44.456 --> 00:18:47.593 align:start size:94% position:6%
in that little strip mall
area where we ordered

00:18:47.593 --> 00:18:50.829 align:start size:94% position:6%
from one restaurant and
you wanted a cup of coffee

00:18:50.829 --> 00:18:52.498 align:start size:88% position:13%
or you wanted a
cappuccino or something

00:18:52.498 --> 00:18:55.601
but we were sitting outside
a Starbucks, which was closed

00:18:55.601 --> 00:18:58.070
but they told us we
couldn't get coffee

00:18:58.070 --> 00:19:00.239
because Starbucks
owns the strip mall

00:19:00.239 --> 00:19:02.207
and wouldn't allow
them to serve coffee

00:19:02.207 --> 00:19:04.676 align:start size:84% position:16%
even though the
Starbucks was closed.

00:19:04.676 --> 00:19:08.046 align:start position:0%
Like, that's the level of
insanity that we're dealing with

00:19:08.046 --> 00:19:09.181
that at a micro level.

00:19:10.782 --> 00:19:13.819
- Well, it's a great
extent the Corona era

00:19:13.819 --> 00:19:15.687
has allowed lots of bossy people

00:19:15.687 --> 00:19:17.256 align:start size:84% position:16%
to do the stuff
they like the most.

00:19:17.256 --> 00:19:18.490
(chuckles)

00:19:18.490 --> 00:19:21.460 align:start size:84% position:16%
I mean, there are some
people who love to,

00:19:21.460 --> 00:19:24.930
you can notice it in certain
establishments that are open

00:19:24.930 --> 00:19:27.299
there are certain people
who just won't do things

00:19:27.299 --> 00:19:28.534
and you ask them why.

00:19:28.534 --> 00:19:30.769
And they say, 'cause
of Corona and even

00:19:31.937 --> 00:19:33.172 align:start size:84% position:16%
there are quite a
lot of establishment

00:19:33.172 --> 00:19:34.573
so I think it was John
Cleese who said famously

00:19:34.573 --> 00:19:35.974
after doing "Fawlty Towers"

00:19:35.974 --> 00:19:37.442 align:start size:84% position:16%
that the definition
of a bad hotel

00:19:37.442 --> 00:19:40.946
or restaurant was
one run entirely

00:19:40.946 --> 00:19:42.748
for the comfort of the staff.

00:19:44.216 --> 00:19:46.151
And there are quite a lot
of establishments, I think

00:19:46.151 --> 00:19:49.021
unwisely for that
future, which have,

00:19:49.021 --> 00:19:50.656
I mean airlines and
lots of other things

00:19:50.656 --> 00:19:52.691 align:start size:97% position:3%
which are doing lots of things
that are quite comfortable

00:19:52.691 --> 00:19:54.092
for the staff

00:19:54.092 --> 00:19:56.762 align:start size:97% position:3%
but make things extra
unpleasant for the clientele.

00:19:56.762 --> 00:20:01.233
But no the bigger
problem you have is

00:20:03.068 --> 00:20:04.603 align:start size:81% position:19%
you just can't
agree on anything.

00:20:04.603 --> 00:20:06.371
You didn't agree on the virus

00:20:06.371 --> 00:20:08.907
and didn't agree on
any response to it.

00:20:08.907 --> 00:20:13.478
And now we have absolutely
ground zero of this problem.

00:20:13.478 --> 00:20:14.313
Can I by the way
say very quickly?

00:20:14.313 --> 00:20:15.247
- Yeah

00:20:15.247 --> 00:20:17.449
- There's only one other thing

00:20:17.449 --> 00:20:21.520 align:start size:97% position:3%
of similar gravity I've seen
in a developed democracy

00:20:21.520 --> 00:20:24.189 align:start size:94% position:6% line:0%
which is a very small
thing that a lot of people

00:20:24.189 --> 00:20:25.857 align:start size:84% position:16% line:0%
didn't take any
notice of at the time.

00:20:25.857 --> 00:20:29.828 align:start position:0% line:0%
But it's two years ago in a
town called Chemnitz in Germany

00:20:30.996 --> 00:20:34.633 align:start size:84% position:16%
there was a video
released by actually

00:20:34.633 --> 00:20:37.336 align:start position:0%
as it happens an Antifa account
that had just cropped up

00:20:37.336 --> 00:20:39.137
could well have been a
disinformation account

00:20:39.137 --> 00:20:40.706
nobody quite knows.

00:20:40.706 --> 00:20:43.775 align:start size:81% position:19%
It showed some
German looking men

00:20:43.775 --> 00:20:46.278
and some migrant looking men.

00:20:46.278 --> 00:20:51.250 align:start size:94% position:6%
And the account said that
it was a migrant hunt

00:20:52.017 --> 00:20:52.985
that was happening.

00:20:52.985 --> 00:20:54.253
It was a very serious thing.

00:20:54.253 --> 00:20:56.088
They'd been a stabbing
and by a bio migrant

00:20:56.088 --> 00:20:58.090
of a local only a
few days earlier

00:20:58.090 --> 00:20:59.992 align:start size:84% position:16%
tensions in the
area were very high.

00:20:59.992 --> 00:21:03.328
This video was released
by an anonymous account.

00:21:03.328 --> 00:21:05.931
And by hours after the
release of the video,

00:21:05.931 --> 00:21:08.734 align:start size:97% position:3%
the German Chancellor
Angela Merkel said publicly,

00:21:08.734 --> 00:21:10.202
" We cannot allow this

00:21:10.202 --> 00:21:12.904
the hunting of human
beings in Germany.

00:21:12.904 --> 00:21:15.474
The reason I tell you this
story is because of this

00:21:16.608 --> 00:21:19.044 align:start size:88% position:13%
the head of the Domestic
Intelligence Service

00:21:19.044 --> 00:21:22.247
in Germany said publicly,

00:21:22.247 --> 00:21:24.483
" No, it doesn't show that."

00:21:25.951 --> 00:21:28.253
Hans-Georg Maaßen the man
who was the most important,

00:21:28.253 --> 00:21:29.921 align:start size:88% position:13%
the head of the Domestic
Intelligence Service

00:21:29.921 --> 00:21:31.790
disagreed with the Chancellor.

00:21:31.790 --> 00:21:32.624
He said,

00:21:32.624 --> 00:21:35.761
" No, it's not that."

00:21:35.761 --> 00:21:37.195
Now there's a dispute

00:21:37.195 --> 00:21:39.698 align:start size:97% position:3%
he was actually was dismissed
from his post that week

00:21:39.698 --> 00:21:40.532
- Wow

00:21:41.667 --> 00:21:42.701
- Now but exactly.

00:21:42.701 --> 00:21:44.069
I wrote about at
the time I said,

00:21:44.069 --> 00:21:47.072
look irrespective of
the details or exactly

00:21:47.072 --> 00:21:48.907
what it is that's going on,

00:21:48.907 --> 00:21:51.410
this should be a
real warning moment

00:21:51.410 --> 00:21:53.478
because we haven't had,

00:21:53.478 --> 00:21:55.047 align:start size:84% position:16%
we've had a case
where people disagree

00:21:55.047 --> 00:21:58.116 align:start size:84% position:16%
about how you
interpret documents

00:21:58.116 --> 00:22:00.085
or sources and all
sorts of things.

00:22:00.085 --> 00:22:01.653 align:start size:84% position:16%
But for the Chancellor
and the Head

00:22:01.653 --> 00:22:04.089
of the Intelligence
Service to disagree

00:22:04.089 --> 00:22:07.959
over a piece of footage
is very, very worrying.

00:22:07.959 --> 00:22:11.296
Then we come to 2020 in America.

00:22:11.296 --> 00:22:15.701 align:start size:97% position:3%
More than eight out of 10
Trump voters in the last poll

00:22:15.701 --> 00:22:18.236
I saw believe Donald
Trump won the election.

00:22:19.638 --> 00:22:23.041
And obviously Joe Biden's
voters believe he won.

00:22:23.041 --> 00:22:27.813 align:start size:97% position:3%
This seems to me a very
perilous moment for democracy.

00:22:27.813 --> 00:22:31.983
It's what I just described in
cabinets on a national level

00:22:31.983 --> 00:22:34.986
you saw the same thing

00:22:34.986 --> 00:22:37.589
and you've come away with
different conclusions.

00:22:37.589 --> 00:22:39.825 align:start size:94% position:6%
- What do you think would
be a responsible way

00:22:39.825 --> 00:22:41.727 align:start size:84% position:16%
for the media to
talk about this then?

00:22:41.727 --> 00:22:43.261
'Cause one of the things
I've been trying to do

00:22:43.261 --> 00:22:45.097
for the last couple of
weeks here is I'm saying,

00:22:45.097 --> 00:22:48.633 align:start size:84% position:16%
look I don't know
exactly what happened.

00:22:48.633 --> 00:22:50.168 align:start size:84% position:16%
I don't think
anyone really knows.

00:22:50.168 --> 00:22:54.139 align:start size:94% position:6%
I do know that at about
midnight Pacific time here

00:22:54.139 --> 00:22:56.742 align:start size:97% position:3%
that about eight States
that Trump had healthy leads

00:22:56.742 --> 00:22:59.277
in all stopped voting
at the same exact time.

00:22:59.277 --> 00:23:01.313
I'm not saying Trump won

00:23:01.313 --> 00:23:02.547
Now it's going to
go to the courts

00:23:02.547 --> 00:23:04.082
and there's all sorts
of things happening

00:23:04.082 --> 00:23:06.485
but I've at least
been trying to talk

00:23:06.485 --> 00:23:08.320
about it respectfully, right.

00:23:08.320 --> 00:23:11.790 align:start position:0%
So that it allows people to
say, okay let the process work.

00:23:11.790 --> 00:23:13.925
And then at the end, if
it comes out that yes

00:23:13.925 --> 00:23:15.127
did I want Trump win to win?

00:23:15.127 --> 00:23:18.096
Yes but if the courts
look at everything

00:23:18.096 --> 00:23:19.898 align:start size:81% position:19%
and he doesn't
win then so be it.

00:23:19.898 --> 00:23:21.867
But I think what a lot
of people are frustrated

00:23:21.867 --> 00:23:24.202
that that eight out of
10, you just referenced,

00:23:24.202 --> 00:23:25.670
I think what they're seeing is

00:23:25.670 --> 00:23:28.306
that the media won't even
let you talk about it.

00:23:28.306 --> 00:23:29.708
And that if you talk about it

00:23:29.708 --> 00:23:31.410
you're gonna be put on a list

00:23:31.410 --> 00:23:33.578 align:start size:97% position:3%
and you're gonna be labeled
a conspiracy theorist

00:23:33.578 --> 00:23:35.647 align:start size:88% position:13%
and you're gonna get
booted from social media

00:23:35.647 --> 00:23:36.915
and the rest of it.

00:23:36.915 --> 00:23:38.383
And that strikes me
as more of a problem

00:23:38.383 --> 00:23:41.553
maybe then what actually
happened at some level.

00:23:41.553 --> 00:23:44.322
- Well no, I disagree with that.

00:23:44.322 --> 00:23:47.626
I mean, I think the
biggest problem is

00:23:47.626 --> 00:23:50.595 align:start size:88% position:13%
if the president doesn't
leave the White House

00:23:50.595 --> 00:23:51.863 align:start size:94% position:6%
and he's lost, I mean this
is the biggest problem.

00:23:51.863 --> 00:23:54.032
- Oh, well of course
that if we get there

00:23:54.032 --> 00:23:57.469
and he has actually lost and
he doesn't leave of course.

00:23:57.469 --> 00:24:00.906
- I mean, you know,
look I'm sympathetic

00:24:00.906 --> 00:24:02.841
to much of your argument on this

00:24:02.841 --> 00:24:05.510
and your point of view
on this but I mean the

00:24:05.510 --> 00:24:08.013
And I'm by the way
I'm particularly
irate about the fact

00:24:08.013 --> 00:24:12.384 align:start size:97% position:3%
that there were so many
Democrats who spent four years

00:24:12.384 --> 00:24:14.252 align:start size:84% position:16%
claiming that the
American voting system

00:24:14.252 --> 00:24:15.787 align:start size:84% position:16%
had been fundamentally
undermined

00:24:15.787 --> 00:24:18.623
and indeed that the Russians
had stolen the 2016 election

00:24:18.623 --> 00:24:20.859 align:start size:97% position:3%
something for which they
never showed us any evidence

00:24:20.859 --> 00:24:22.027
but they asserted anyway.

00:24:22.027 --> 00:24:24.062 align:start size:84% position:16%
- Nancy Pelosi
literally said that

00:24:24.062 --> 00:24:27.566
that it was an illegitimate
election, I mean, its yeah

00:24:27.566 --> 00:24:29.835
- I'm irate about that.

00:24:29.835 --> 00:24:31.369
I was irate about
it for four years.

00:24:31.369 --> 00:24:32.971
I'm irate about the fact that
these same people now pretend

00:24:32.971 --> 00:24:36.875
that there is no such thing
as voter fraud in America.

00:24:36.875 --> 00:24:41.112
However, the owners at this
stage is on Donald Trump

00:24:41.112 --> 00:24:44.616
and his legal team to prove
that he won the election.

00:24:44.616 --> 00:24:48.553
Now I have to say, I've paid
fairly close attention to this.

00:24:48.553 --> 00:24:52.157
As I say, first of all may I
say, the thing of going to bed

00:24:52.157 --> 00:24:53.892 align:start size:94% position:6%
and the result being
different when you wake up

00:24:53.892 --> 00:24:56.061
is not unheard of in elections.

00:24:56.061 --> 00:24:58.697
I mean in the Brexit vote,

00:24:58.697 --> 00:25:01.333
lots of people went
to bed thinking that

00:25:02.767 --> 00:25:04.870 align:start size:97% position:3%
that Britain was going to
remain in the European Union

00:25:04.870 --> 00:25:06.404
I remember it very clearly.

00:25:06.404 --> 00:25:09.841
And of course then suddenly
the results from Sunderland

00:25:09.841 --> 00:25:11.276 align:start size:94% position:6%
and elsewhere in the North
of England came through

00:25:11.276 --> 00:25:13.011
and whoosh we were out

00:25:13.011 --> 00:25:16.381
and the same people woke
up the next morning amazed

00:25:16.381 --> 00:25:18.917
but that's what happens
sometimes in elections.

00:25:20.051 --> 00:25:22.888 align:start size:84% position:16%
I do think that Donald
Trump is behaving

00:25:22.888 --> 00:25:24.222
reprehensibly at the moment.

00:25:24.222 --> 00:25:29.194
I think that frankly,
I am very open for any

00:25:29.194 --> 00:25:31.396 align:start size:84% position:16%
and all explanations
of voter fraud

00:25:31.396 --> 00:25:34.432 align:start size:94% position:6%
as it is going on in
America as it has gone on.

00:25:34.432 --> 00:25:38.537
I think whoever is president
on January the 20th rather

00:25:38.537 --> 00:25:43.074 align:start size:97% position:3%
as a point of absolute
urgency should put together

00:25:43.074 --> 00:25:46.878 align:start size:88% position:13%
a bipartisan nonpartisan
cross partisan team

00:25:46.878 --> 00:25:48.980
to look into voter
fraud, specifically

00:25:48.980 --> 00:25:51.082
mail-in voter fraud in the
United States of America.

00:25:51.082 --> 00:25:54.419
You cannot have another
election after this one

00:25:54.419 --> 00:25:56.121
which would be a third
in a row where people

00:25:56.121 --> 00:25:58.156
didn't believe the
results if they lost.

00:25:58.156 --> 00:26:01.259 align:start size:94% position:6%
So it seems to me to be
real point of urgency this

00:26:01.259 --> 00:26:04.930 align:start size:94% position:6%
but on election night,
when Donald Trump came out

00:26:04.930 --> 00:26:07.032
in the early hours of
the morning and said

00:26:08.433 --> 00:26:10.635
"I believe we've already won.

00:26:10.635 --> 00:26:12.571
"We've won as far
as I'm concerned,"

00:26:12.571 --> 00:26:13.371
he said.

00:26:13.371 --> 00:26:14.806
I gasped, I gasped.

00:26:14.806 --> 00:26:17.309
I thought, oh hell.

00:26:17.309 --> 00:26:19.311
And there's several
things about that.

00:26:19.311 --> 00:26:23.081
One is you better, if
you're the Trump team

00:26:23.081 --> 00:26:26.484 align:start size:97% position:3%
you better provide really
good proof, fast about that.

00:26:26.484 --> 00:26:29.220
And frankly what
they've provided

00:26:29.220 --> 00:26:31.389
is not good enough proof yet.

00:26:31.389 --> 00:26:35.961 align:start size:97% position:3%
They have been providing
some things that sound to me

00:26:35.961 --> 00:26:38.363 align:start size:84% position:16%
like they are
conspiracy theories

00:26:38.363 --> 00:26:39.965
unless they've got a
lot of stuff to come.

00:26:39.965 --> 00:26:42.100 align:start size:97% position:3%
I hope for their sake, they've
got a lot of stuff to come

00:26:42.100 --> 00:26:43.568 align:start size:81% position:19%
or there are a
lot of reputations

00:26:43.568 --> 00:26:45.470 align:start size:84% position:16%
that are being
trashed all the time

00:26:45.470 --> 00:26:46.705
(mumbles)

00:26:46.705 --> 00:26:47.505
- Well, that's what
I said from B one.

00:26:47.505 --> 00:26:48.807
It's like Sidney Powell.

00:26:48.807 --> 00:26:50.275 align:start size:97% position:3%
She's either self-immolating
in front of us

00:26:50.275 --> 00:26:52.811 align:start size:88% position:13%
or she's about to break
the greatest story

00:26:52.811 --> 00:26:54.813
in the history of modern times.

00:26:54.813 --> 00:26:56.047
It's one or the other, right?

00:26:56.047 --> 00:26:59.484 align:start size:84% position:16%
- Yeah and I suspect
it's the first.

00:26:59.484 --> 00:27:02.287
And I think the same
with Rudy Giuliani.

00:27:02.287 --> 00:27:05.256 align:start size:94% position:6%
You just can't give
press conferences talking

00:27:05.256 --> 00:27:07.359
about dead Venezuelan leaders

00:27:08.793 --> 00:27:12.097
and think that the citizenry
should, I mean, it's not just

00:27:12.097 --> 00:27:14.599
that you shouldn't treat
the citizenry stupidly,

00:27:14.599 --> 00:27:18.637
you should not miss the
lead people's belief

00:27:18.637 --> 00:27:21.239
in the most fundamental
thing in our nations

00:27:21.239 --> 00:27:22.474
which is that we vote

00:27:22.474 --> 00:27:23.942
and some people win and
some people lose them

00:27:23.942 --> 00:27:26.845
and you know who's
lost and who's won.

00:27:26.845 --> 00:27:29.314
This is a really
dangerous thing.

00:27:29.314 --> 00:27:32.384 align:start size:97% position:3%
This is a dangerous
element to be playing with.

00:27:32.384 --> 00:27:36.421
And I worry deeply about
the consequences of this.

00:27:36.421 --> 00:27:39.324 align:start size:88% position:13%
But another thing to
point out about this is,

00:27:40.525 --> 00:27:44.496
that I mean, everyone
has to lose sometimes

00:27:44.496 --> 00:27:46.765
I remember Michael
Barone saying this

00:27:46.765 --> 00:27:50.035 align:start size:97% position:3%
to some conservative gathering
I once sat many years ago.

00:27:50.035 --> 00:27:52.771 align:start size:97% position:3%
I think when Obama won,
Michael Barone said, you know

00:27:52.771 --> 00:27:54.806
you have to lose some times.

00:27:57.208 --> 00:28:01.012
The evidence so far seems to
be that the Republican nominee

00:28:01.012 --> 00:28:03.415 align:start size:81% position:19%
for the presidency
lost this time.

00:28:03.415 --> 00:28:06.418 align:start size:84% position:16%
Now here's the kicker
if I may say so

00:28:07.252 --> 00:28:08.953
For four years,

00:28:10.989 --> 00:28:12.257
one of the questions has been

00:28:12.257 --> 00:28:14.826
why has Donald Trump
not been able to ...

00:28:14.826 --> 00:28:17.262
Now, there have been some
very remarkable people

00:28:17.262 --> 00:28:18.496
who have worked for him.

00:28:18.496 --> 00:28:19.998 align:start size:84% position:16%
And I wouldn't do
that in any of them.

00:28:19.998 --> 00:28:22.033
I'm thinking of people like,
I think Secretary of State

00:28:22.033 --> 00:28:24.903 align:start size:84% position:16%
Mike Pompeo, Elliott
Abrams and others

00:28:27.706 --> 00:28:30.508 align:start size:84% position:16%
some very very
serious particular
foreign policy figures

00:28:30.508 --> 00:28:32.777
who have worked for him
and I deeply admire,

00:28:32.777 --> 00:28:33.945
but there has been a question

00:28:33.945 --> 00:28:35.480
throughout the Trump presidency.

00:28:35.480 --> 00:28:40.318
Why can he not appear to get
more people working with him

00:28:42.887 --> 00:28:46.191 align:start size:97% position:3%
more experienced people
working for him, older hands

00:28:46.191 --> 00:28:50.595
more trusted figures, some
non-family would be nice

00:28:51.496 --> 00:28:52.597
and so on and so forth.

00:28:52.597 --> 00:28:53.832
What is the explanation?

00:28:53.832 --> 00:28:57.102
And it's one of those
political questions

00:28:57.102 --> 00:28:58.703
that ends up answering itself.

00:28:58.703 --> 00:29:02.507
It's because everyone worried
that at the end of the run,

00:29:02.507 --> 00:29:05.443 align:start size:81% position:19%
he would pull some
crap like this.

00:29:05.443 --> 00:29:07.645
That was why, that was why

00:29:07.645 --> 00:29:11.349
I spoke to a lot of people
in recent years in America

00:29:11.349 --> 00:29:15.487 align:start size:94% position:6%
and said to them and
American friends and said,

00:29:15.487 --> 00:29:17.789
would you consider
taking this post?

00:29:17.789 --> 00:29:19.524 align:start size:84% position:16%
Why don't you consider
taking that role?

00:29:19.524 --> 00:29:22.293 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I always noticed that
some of them early on

00:29:22.293 --> 00:29:25.730 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I would say, he's
got four years in office.

00:29:25.730 --> 00:29:27.232
It's not nothing to be

00:29:27.232 --> 00:29:29.667 align:start size:84% position:16%
whatever position
was being discussed.

00:29:29.667 --> 00:29:31.803 align:start size:84% position:16%
And I noticed always
this reticence,

00:29:31.803 --> 00:29:35.340
I think Neil Ferguson
on your show said that

00:29:35.340 --> 00:29:36.574
there was always this risk

00:29:36.574 --> 00:29:38.076 align:start size:81% position:19%
that Trump was
gonna do something

00:29:38.076 --> 00:29:40.945
or come down in a way
that was a scandal

00:29:41.846 --> 00:29:43.681
of not any Nixonian proportions

00:29:43.681 --> 00:29:45.617
but it would make
Nixon look like,

00:29:45.617 --> 00:29:48.887 align:start size:88% position:13%
as sort of a tea party,
no tea party means

00:29:48.887 --> 00:29:49.821
something else I
didn't mean anyway

00:29:49.821 --> 00:29:50.755
- That means something else does

00:29:50.755 --> 00:29:52.757
Not a British tea but well

00:29:52.757 --> 00:29:53.925
- Yeah yeah.

00:29:53.925 --> 00:29:55.460 align:start size:84% position:16%
- A British tea
party of another turn

00:29:55.460 --> 00:29:56.327
- A cake walk, a cake walk, a
cake walk, I think that, yeah.

00:29:56.327 --> 00:29:57.595
- Cakewalk, yeah

00:29:57.595 --> 00:30:02.167
- And I think that
what we're seeing

00:30:03.368 --> 00:30:05.603
at the moment may be the
answer to that question.

00:30:05.603 --> 00:30:08.206
I have seen it once
else in politics

00:30:08.206 --> 00:30:11.109
in European continental
politics with a much

00:30:11.109 --> 00:30:14.212
more minor political figure
who the same question was

00:30:14.212 --> 00:30:16.114
why can't people
cohere around him?

00:30:16.114 --> 00:30:17.348
Why don't people trust him?

00:30:17.348 --> 00:30:20.285 align:start size:84% position:16%
And in the end, the
answer answered itself

00:30:20.285 --> 00:30:22.220 align:start size:84% position:16%
because he was
going to in the end

00:30:22.220 --> 00:30:24.589
pull the crazy crappy he pulled,

00:30:24.589 --> 00:30:29.027
And I just, I think that unless

00:30:30.295 --> 00:30:32.997
the Trump team can
very very swiftly

00:30:32.997 --> 00:30:37.068
provide evidence that is
very good and persuasive,

00:30:37.068 --> 00:30:38.603
they are playing

00:30:38.603 --> 00:30:41.172
with an element that they
should not be playing with.

00:30:41.172 --> 00:30:43.041
And I think it will

00:30:43.041 --> 00:30:46.411
it will deeply diminish
the Republican Party

00:30:46.411 --> 00:30:48.780
if it allows it to go on, it
will diminish conservatives.

00:30:48.780 --> 00:30:51.449
It will diminish the
millions and millions

00:30:51.449 --> 00:30:53.685 align:start size:94% position:6%
of decent American
voters who were trying to

00:30:53.685 --> 00:30:56.788 align:start size:84% position:16%
send a very distinct
message in 2016

00:30:56.788 --> 00:31:00.191 align:start size:97% position:3%
who were reviled for four
years, insulted for four years

00:31:00.191 --> 00:31:02.594
called every imaginable
name in for four years

00:31:02.594 --> 00:31:07.599 align:start size:94% position:6%
it will further demoralize
them and weaken them.

00:31:08.900 --> 00:31:11.769 align:start size:97% position:3%
I hope if he has something,
it comes out fast.

00:31:11.769 --> 00:31:13.238
- Yeah by the way,
Douglas, you know

00:31:13.238 --> 00:31:16.040 align:start size:97% position:3%
while I'm obviously
sympathetic to the campaign

00:31:16.040 --> 00:31:18.276
and I wanted him to win, I'm
completely with you on that.

00:31:18.276 --> 00:31:20.578
It's like if there
isn't anything there

00:31:20.578 --> 00:31:23.748
and they've truly
done something here

00:31:23.748 --> 00:31:25.717
that was to destroy the system

00:31:25.717 --> 00:31:27.518 align:start size:88% position:13%
or completely erode
trust or anything else,

00:31:27.518 --> 00:31:30.021 align:start size:94% position:6%
yeah then it's almost
the most dangerous thing.

00:31:30.021 --> 00:31:32.724
Well, I guess it would be the
second, most dangerous thing

00:31:32.724 --> 00:31:34.893
compared to actually
rigging the election.

00:31:34.893 --> 00:31:38.429
So we'll find out over
the next couple of weeks.

00:31:38.429 --> 00:31:39.864
- If they have

00:31:39.864 --> 00:31:41.366 align:start size:94% position:6%
if you Democrats did
actually rig the election

00:31:41.366 --> 00:31:43.768
then it is indeed it is
the most appalling crime

00:31:43.768 --> 00:31:45.303
against American democracy.

00:31:45.303 --> 00:31:50.108
And there should be such
a thorough investigation

00:31:50.108 --> 00:31:53.144
and so many people
going to prison.

00:31:53.144 --> 00:31:56.381 align:start size:88% position:13%
It would be the scandal
of our lifetimes.

00:31:56.381 --> 00:32:00.251 align:start size:94% position:6% line:0%
But if it isn't the case,
if it isn't the case

00:32:00.251 --> 00:32:02.287 line:0%
then it is also a great scandal

00:32:02.287 --> 00:32:05.156
because you cannot lie to
the citizen about this.

00:32:05.156 --> 00:32:08.293 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm very open to the
argument of four years ago

00:32:08.293 --> 00:32:10.461 align:start size:84% position:16%
Hillary Clinton didn't
really admit that

00:32:10.461 --> 00:32:12.997
she lost the election and
spent years pretending she

00:32:12.997 --> 00:32:14.832
had only lost election
because of the Russians

00:32:14.832 --> 00:32:17.101 align:start size:88% position:13%
and something to do
with a box on Facebook.

00:32:18.269 --> 00:32:20.505 align:start size:84% position:16%
Look, I thought that
was contemptible.

00:32:20.505 --> 00:32:22.240
I think Hillary
Clinton was again

00:32:22.240 --> 00:32:25.343 align:start size:97% position:3%
playing with fire to do
her the one piece of credit

00:32:25.343 --> 00:32:26.878
that one can do.

00:32:26.878 --> 00:32:29.747
At least she didn't actually
tunnel into the Oval Office

00:32:29.747 --> 00:32:33.284
